    "result_text": "All tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other two files are an abstract base and a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` derived attribute so the application satisfies the spec: **`riskFlag` is `true` when any of these hold \u2014 the owner is a possible duplicate, the email domain is disposable-adjacent, or the city is over its soft capacity; otherwise `false`.**\n\nChanges, following the existing derived-attribute conventions:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` field (`@Column(name = \"risk_flag\")`) with getter/setter, next to the existing `possibleDuplicate` fields.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `riskFlag` (readOnly boolean) property to the Owner schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto.riskFlag`, which MapStruct maps automatically by name.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 set `riskFlag` at the end of `assignDerivedAttributes(...)`, reusing the already-computed flags plus a new helper:\n   - `isRiskFlagged(owner)` = `possibleDuplicate` **OR** disposable-adjacent email **OR** `capacityWarning` (the city's soft-capacity band, 40\u201349, already computed by `isCityApproachingCapacity`).\n   - `isDisposableAdjacentEmail(email)` \u2014 true when the email domain is a *subdomain* of a known disposable domain (e.g. `x.mailinator.com`). Exactly-disposable domains are already rejected with 400 during validation, so this \"adjacent\" band is the meaningful, distinct case; a null/empty email is not adjacent.\n\n4. **`db/{h2,hsqldb,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `risk_flag` column to the `owners` table (required, or persistence fails with a 500 \u2014 which is what the first test run surfaced).\n\nThe one acceptance test (`coreRiskFlagFalseNormally`) \u2014 a fully-unique owner with no email, a unique city, and no duplicate \u2014 correctly yields `riskFlag = false`.\n\nOne interpretation worth flagging: the spec's three conditions map onto pre-existing derived flags \u2014 \"possible duplicate\" \u2192 `possibleDuplicate`, and \"over its soft capacity\" \u2192 the `capacityWarning` band (40\u201349, below the hard cap of 50). \"Disposable-adjacent\" had no prior definition, so I defined it as a subdomain of a blocklisted disposable domain (exact matches are already rejected pre-creation). The only test pins the all-false case; if you intended different thresholds for these bands, let me know and I'll adjust.",
